From 2e3957029e5a91d6b527deeb5b399124408baefd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scroll Ash Lab <scrollash.lab@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:35:16 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] find_valid_patches: do not scale plain zarr arrays as if
 multiscale

Plain zarr Arrays have no multiscale levels. Requesting
valid_patch_find_resolution >= 1 previously treated the full-resolution
array as already downsampled and multiplied patch starts by 2**level,
writing out-of-bounds positions into the patch cache (#1970).

For objects without group keys, _resolve_resolution now only satisfies
level 0; higher levels return None so the existing full-resolution
fallback runs. OME-Zarr groups are unchanged.

Diagnosis and fix direction: @mg255 on ScrollPrize/villa#1970.
---
 .../models/datasets/find_valid_patches.py     |  55 ++++--
 .../test_find_valid_patches_resolution.py     | 162 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 202 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)
